### Create an order - this saves to MongoDB AND publishes a RabbitMQ event
POST http://localhost:8080/orders/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "p1",
  "customerId": "cust2",
  "quantity": 3,
  "price": 99.98
}

### Watch Inventory Service's console after sending the request above - you
### should see a line like:
### Message Received from queue: {orderId=..., productId=p1, quantity=2}
###
### Order Service has no idea whether Inventory Service is even running -
### it published the event and moved on. That's the whole point.

### Check the order was actually saved (replace <id> with the id from the response above)
GET http://localhost:8080/orders/6a661c2e3782bad36790a7dc
